  "guidelines": {
    "cell": "B151",
    "text": "As a standard practice, Please make a note of following : 1. 1 No COM Board per Cubicle Max 40 AEB configuration can be done in COM Board, PSC quantity can be decided as per technical requirement. 2. AEB Boards and BSI are always equal to No of Wheel Sensors 3. In metros, No need to consider deflector Plates. 4. For single detetion system , maximum we will go with BP-EXB-1 and BP-EXB-2 5. For Dual detetion system , maximum we will go with BP-EXB-4 6. 15U Cubicle- 4 IO-Exb and only one BGT with switches 7. 20U Cubicle- 10 IO-Exb and 2 BGT with switches. 8. 35U Cubicle- 20 IO-exb and 4 BGT with switches. 9. Reset Box Qty : For Station : equal to No of Track section and For automatic block section : each line, each system can have one reset Box 10. Reset cubicle: For station : maximum 22 reset box can be accomodated. 11. Reset cooperative panel : for station and auto block , IBH, ABSOLUTE- maximum 6 reset box can be accomodated with 2 cooperation Key 12. For supervisory track section , FDS is mandatory 13. 1 FDS equal to 110 participants(Maximum Limit) 14. For data transimission : 3 vital inputs can be sent through one IO in Quad mode and 6 non -vital inputs can be sent through one IO in Dual mode. 12 non -vital inputs can be sent through one IO in Single mode. Accordingly we should calcuate the Qty of IO-EXB for data transmission. 1 AEB Can maximum sent 24 arguments 15. 1 No of IO-EXB will be for output 2 track section 16. Cable Length if not specified in tender document. For Station Application : 1) For single detection -(75% of 5 Metre, 15% of 10 Metre and 10 % of 15 Metre) 2) Dual Detection System , for redundant system (75% of 10 Metre for redundant system , 25% of 15 Metre) and (75% of 5 Metre, 15% of 10 Metre and 10 % of 15 Metre) for non redundant system(main system) For Auto Block Application : ( 50% of 5 Metre, 50% of 10 Metre ) FOR IBH Application : 1) For single detection all with 5 Metre 2) For dual detection - 50% of 5 Metre, 50% of 10 Metre For ABSOLUTE BLOCK: 1)For single detection all with 5 Metre 2) For dual detection -( 50% of 5 Metre, 50% of 10 Metre ) 17. Rail Claw: 1) Indian Railways : 60Kg (assumption) -Internal and the same shall be confirmed by the project team at the time of execution 2)For Metros : We use Rail Claw SK 140-010(for Metros). For Ballast track , we have to consider 60 KG(Indian Rail Profile). 18. Protection tube flame resistant should be used for Metro projects. For indian Railway projects we use Normal Protection Tube 19. Communication Board COM-AdC101 should be used for Relay interface projects. Communication board COM-FSE101 is for standard interface/Hitachi/ Kyosan for serial interface project . Communication board COM-FSFB is for serial interface projects for Alstom 20. Frauscher diagnostic system FDS101 SNMP- for alstom projects 21. Frauscher diagnostic system FDS102 for other Projects. 22. For Station Application , Please consider switch with out SFP in case of centralized application. 23. LV BOX are always considered (equal) for Point zone Track circuits or as per tender requirement/ as per Zonal railway Policy, Applicable for station application. 24. Ethernet Switches are to be considered as per tender requirement or scope is not clear than go with OFC ethernet OFC switches. IN EPC tender for auto block consider L3 Switch for stations and L2 switches for ALH/ RH/LSC."
  },
